```yaml
spec:
  grid: 20-30 rows x 17-30 cols, black background
  objects: 2-4 green (3) hollow rectangular outlines, non-overlapping
  outline_shape:
    frame: rectangular perimeter (border-only), height 3-5, width 3-6
    tab: exactly 1 extra green pixel protruding outward from the midpoint of one side
    tab_axis_length: must be odd (so midpoint is integer); perpendicular axis >=3
    tab_sides_used: each of left/right/top/bottom used at most once per example [observed]
  transform:
    mirror_axis: determined by tab side; reflection placed on the opposite side with 1-cell gap
    color: left/right tab => blue (1) horizontal mirror; top/bottom tab => teal (8) vertical mirror
    clipping: reflection may extend beyond grid edge; visible portion is painted, rest is clipped
    no_overlap: reflections must land entirely on background (no collision with any green object or other reflection)
  spacing: objects and their reflections must have >=1 background cell separating all bboxes

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size in range.
    2. For each of N=2-4 objects, generate a rectangular frame (h in 3-5, w in 3-6) and pick a tab side (left/right/top/bottom). Ensure the tab-parallel dimension is odd. Attach a 1-pixel tab at the midpoint of that side.
    3. Compute the mirrored copy (flipped LR for left/right tab, UD for top/bottom) and its placement offset (bbox opposite edge + 2).
    4. Place the (object + reflection) pair on the grid as a unit, ensuring no overlap with previously placed pairs and that the green object bbox is within bounds. The reflection may be partially clipped by the grid edge.
    5. Return only the green objects (input); the reflections form the output delta.
```
